  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation (config_006, acc=0.653) is the clear best so far, while image-only models (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227) are very weak in isolation. The critical open question is whether the weak image modality provides complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA modality, or whether it adds only noise. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_006—the only difference is the addition of the image branch with simple concat fusion. If it fails to beat 0.653, we can confidently deprioritize all multimodal configs and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements. If it does help, it opens the fusion-method and image-encoder dimensions for further exploration. Choosing concat over weighted keeps the fusion assumption minimal, and resnet50 (already characterized) over ViT-L avoids introducing two new variables at once."
}

